  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. Yara wants to change her outgoing flight to a nonstop flight the next day and move her return flight back by a day. First, I need to check the current flights in her reservation. The outgoing flights are HAT085 from IAH to JFK on May 18th and HAT023 from JFK to SFO the same day. The return is HAT278 from SFO to IAH on May 22nd.\n\nShe wants the outgoing to be nonstop the next day, so May 19th. I need to search for direct flights from IAH to SFO on May 19th. Wait, the original outgoing is a two-leg flight (IAH to JFK to SFO). A nonstop would be IAH to SFO. So I should use the search_direct_flight function for origin IAH, destination SFO, date 2024-05-19. Also, check the return flight. She wants to move the return back by a day, so from May 22nd to May 23rd. So search for direct flights from SFO to IAH on May 23rd. But she specified departing after 8am and before 9pm. Need to ensure the flights found are within that time window.\n\nOnce I have the new flights, I can proceed to update the reservation. Since she has insurance, any fees should be waived. Then, after modifying the flights, she wants to upgrade to business class and add 2 checked bags, willing to pay up to $200. If the upgrade cost is more, she's okay with keeping economy on the return. If that's not possible, economy for both legs but add the bags. The original payment was a gift card, so need to use that for any additional charges.\n\nFirst step: Search for direct flights for the outgoing on May 19th and return on May 23rd. Let me call the search_direct_flight function for each leg.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"search_direct_flight\", \"arguments\": {\"origin\": \"IAH\", \"destination\": \"SFO\", \"date\": \"2024-05-19\"}}\n",
  "continuation_text": " day. First, I need to check the current flights in her reservation. The outgoing flights are HAT085 from IAH to JFK on May 18th and HAT023 from JFK to SFO the same day. The return is HAT278 from SFO to IAH on May 22nd.\n\nShe wants the outgoing to be nonstop the next day, so May 19th. I need to search for direct flights from IAH to SFO on May 19th. Wait, the original outgoing is a two-leg flight (IAH to JFK to SFO). A nonstop would be IAH to SFO. So I should use the search_direct_flight function for origin IAH, destination SFO, date 2024-05-19. Also, check the return flight. She wants to move the return back by a day, so from May 22nd to May 23rd. So search for direct flights from SFO to IAH on May 23rd. But she specified departing after 8am and before 9pm. Need to ensure the flights found are within that time window.\n\nOnce I have the new flights, I can proceed to update the reservation. Since she has insurance, any fees should be waived. Then, after modifying the flights, she wants to upgrade to business class and add 2 checked bags, willing to pay up to $200. If the upgrade cost is more, she's okay with keeping economy on the return. If that's not possible, economy for both legs but add the bags. The original payment was a gift card, so need to use that for any additional charges.\n\nFirst step: Search for direct flights for the outgoing on May 19th and return on May 23rd. Let me call the search_direct_flight function for each leg.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"search_direct_flight\", \"arguments\": {\"origin\": \"IAH\", \"destination\": \"SFO\", \"date\": \"2024-05-19\"}}\n",
